": "Logo Animation and Motion Identity Systems", "description": "This unit shows how motion extends brand identity through animated marks, transitions, mnemonic gestures, sonic identity, and reusable system rules.", "children": [{"id": "d6bff734-21ce-4334-b357-5f4845f6ff13", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Animated marks and logo behavior", "children": [{"id": "cffdd6d0-38a6-4e1d-a00e-11c1e9e23d48", "type": "concept", "title": "logo reveal"}, {"id": "9db79152-a87c-4298-8f91-44963ddea875", "type": "concept", "title": "morph"}, {"id": "4819f4cb-55e6-416b-87fd-ed7e24c638c9", "type": "concept", "title": "build-on"}, {"id": "5976c458-5ece-4192-82e1-b5402342f9d4", "type": "concept", "title": "lockup"}, {"id": "5ec9d3a5-0588-44b4-b9da-74c2b8f54bb2", "type": "concept", "title": "brand mnemonic"}, {"id": "eedc463e-22d1-4f67-9af9-e220ead4a442", "type": "concept", "title": "motion signature"}], "description": "Students learn to animate logos through transformation, assembly, reveal, morphing, and responsive movement."}, {"id": "39075f35-7c60-4e08-bc48-3fd73dbf2140", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Motion brand guidelines", "children": [{"id": "d024faec-42ff-4721-bf3b-3143de049c40", "type": "concept", "title": "motion principle"}, {"id": "4a110942-1d23-4601-9c3e-fc061d99e1b2", "type": "concept", "title": "duration rule"}, {"id": "a7be5120-6cdd-4d2b-a329-d8ad2461deda", "type": "concept", "title": "easing curve"}, {"id": "6a6fd635-fd5c-4e6e-99dd-1fe1eb1cb245", "type": "concept", "title": "transition system"}, {"id": "a1e089c9-30e6-4e69-8951-0aaa31ce7e6a", "type": "concept", "title": "brand behavior"}, {"id": "4d1d5232-c4fb-4b7e-81d0-5fc737a480df", "type": "concept", "title": "usage guideline"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces the rules that keep identity animation consistent across platforms and teams."}, {"id": "9543fa5d-0281-4b08-8f0e-17bfaf126940", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sonic and sensory identity", "children": [{"id": "2040ab25-5f1b-4381-9b41-b36ccf2a536b", "type": "concept", "title": "sonic logo"}, {"id": "f8a97a5c-58ac-4425-96be-30f0ab423c65", "type": "concept", "title": "audio sting"}, {"id": "dbdd8f18-51d0-4941-96f6-ba5494597d14", "type": "concept", "title": "sync point"}, {"id": "195a9fd0-d091-4cd8-aa6a-b61353cd3e32", "type": "concept", "title": "haptic cue"}, {"id": "0942e071-baf0-4f50-9a4c-9a7f16f88129", "type": "concept", "title": "brand tempo"}, {"id": "af016b2a-6ca9-4cd6-bd77-6a5a1e87543e", "type": "concept", "title": "sound mnemonic"}], "description": "Students connect motion to sound logos, micro-sounds, rhythm, and multisensory brand recognition."}]}, {"id": "0f4118e1-76d2-41e1-9b9b-6c488a9fe18a", "type": "topic", "title": "Title Sequences, Openers, and Broadcast Packages", "description": "Title and broadcast design demand strong concept, pacing, typography, image systems, and production polish in a compact time frame.", "children": [{"id": "f6205059-fa2b-4996-ac3f-c6278e964039", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Title sequence concept", "children": [{"id": "e6b191b6-12a3-4b69-91f4-91e5876ec1a3", "type": "concept", "title": "opening titles"}, {"id": "847d6b4d-9b67-4ac5-8ae5-6f212eb9fc7a", "type": "concept", "title": "concept board"}, {"id": "1c269844-5330-4e57-a747-db7677ec592f", "type": "concept", "title": "visual metaphor"}, {"id": "7202d2e0-29fd-4759-a654-6f6f0971ba7e", "type": "concept", "title": "credit hierarchy"}, {"id": "a2f2033b-9865-4070-90ce-1ac9e900d745", "type": "concept", "title": "genre cue"}, {"id": "ecb1fdac-a0be-4699-8b36-2567a51e0684", "type": "concept", "title": "narrative foreshadowing"}], "description": "Students design openings that introduce tone, theme, world, genre, and visual metaphor."}, {"id": "a75acd8c-0128-437e-8495-ecceec23f3a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Broadcast and channel packages", "children": [{"id": "bce8fe65-391e-4a22-934d-a63785d0c073", "type": "concept", "title": "bumper"}, {"id": "3fc95d43-1959-464e-8c35-b49c9dbb468a", "type": "concept", "title": "lower third"}, {"id": "b1076b0f-9789-4332-98b1-8fa503d2cc49", "type": "concept", "title": "bug"}, {"id": "7886cbbf-8744-481b-804b-699d5516080c", "type": "concept", "title": "stinger"}, {"id": "4604a6a9-b156-480a-bcae-835a90e86ba6", "type": "concept", "title": "promo package"}, {"id": "d11f28ff-e3b1-4df0-affd-8ce0a727b660", "type": "concept", "title": "end card"}], "description": "This subtopic covers repeatable motion systems used in television, streaming, sports, news, and digital channels."}, {"id": "b6dcdc95-d955-4e3f-b0da-23257c298cf4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editing rhythm and sequence structure", "children": [{"id": "316a72d6-1c58-4ed0-81ac-9f015f260584", "type": "concept", "title": "beat edit"}, {"id": "a0f47ad9-3abf-4c4c-b220-2b3d65e7ed1b", "type": "concept", "title": "montage"}, {"id": "6b59d325-b8a6-468c-9934-5d01704cbf4b", "type": "concept", "title": "cut point"}, {"id": "d3fc7b6e-5df1-476b-9a2f-d2fe710b5baf", "type": "concept", "title": "arc"}, {"id": "834f179e-9898-40c7-885a-63f1a2d43480", "type": "concept", "title": "crescendo"}, {"id": "2e44c15f-2d9e-47b5-ad2e-0eaf61e0b707", "type": "concept", "title": "resolution frame"}], "description": "Students build sequences that balance legibility, momentum, surprise, and resolution."}]}, {"id": "8398bbbd-99a7-42de-9805-0a56e99326b4", "type": "topic", "title": "Explainer Videos and Information Motion", "description": "Explainers use motion to make ideas, systems, data, and processes easier to understand. This unit links clarity, narrative, diagrams, and pacing.", "children": [{"id": "38b83f4b-334e-47fa-982e-6ac421599967", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Script, audience, and explanation strategy", "children": [{"id": "fba6d706-f808-4c0d-81e3-97c23a499072", "type": "concept", "title": "audience persona"}, {"id": "804ab799-a5bd-4695-bdf6-25959f99c8e1", "type": "concept", "title": "problem statement"}, {"id": "a581e1df-1b16-4084-9db6-7aae81065658", "type": "concept", "title": "voiceover script"}, {"id": "21c6e5ab-4215-4b2c-8808-4728ca3af92f", "type": "concept", "title": "learning objective"}, {"id": "996f65bb-8a65-432b-8366-1783bec23930", "type": "concept", "title": "call to action"}, {"id": "1fc1e88e-4f97-460a-959f-e1db53aa2794", "type": "concept", "title": "message ladder"}], "description": "Students learn to simplify without flattening meaning by defining the viewer, problem, promise, and learning path."}, {"id": "6ca3468f-0fb2-4bb2-b5e2-9e32f4bc6769", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Animated diagrams and data", "children": [{"id": "50f489de-cc07-45d0-8d0c-5851400e388f", "type": "concept", "title": "diagram animation"}, {"id": "3dc9edce-c214-4f0f-8dc0-aba6a094f387", "type": "concept", "title": "chart reveal"}, {"id": "0ad059ad-5d15-4db5-849c-6ec30a0df048", "type": "concept", "title": "data label"}, {"id": "a211ad38-0da7-4a9e-bc42-f5e1a98962e9", "type": "concept", "title": "flow map"}, {"id": "a72885f4-3340-41c3-b9db-8eb1d2e64d4d", "type": "concept", "title": "process step"}, {"id": "e20fe98c-6433-4471-8901-2ce6016e8af9", "type": "concept", "title": "information hierarchy"}], "description": "This subtopic covers visualizing flows, comparisons, timelines, quantities, and systems over time."}, {"id": "fcdd5f68-d03f-4c7a-9937-98dd3f1c8990", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clarity and cognitive load", "children": [{"id": "ce56e70c-28c4-4a2a-bd81-cf0ca860c2cb", "type": "concept", "title": "cognitive load"}, {"id": "23925753-2582-483b-8c66-3677f4797b15", "type": "concept", "title": "chunking"}, {"id": "84061c55-4612-479b-800f-e4a2e0950375", "type": "concept", "title": "progressive disclosure"}, {"id": "eb90d117-1acb-4fe3-b1d5-97d140d52619", "type": "concept", "title": "pace"}, {"id": "8c63eaae-dd1e-4c7c-9516-53872c95856e", "type": "concept", "title": "redundancy"}, {"id": "4a3a952a-a108-483f-a796-32bec3ef2bc0", "type": "concept", "title": "visual simplification"}], "description": "Students manage pacing, labels, screen density, and narration so viewers can process information."}]}, {"id": "962840eb-b8f7-4435-a0b5-6e8beb2537ef", "type": "topic", "title": "Sound, Music, Voice, and Motion Synchronization", "description": "Sound shapes motion perception. Students learn to design with voice, music, silence, effects, rhythm, and synchronization from the start of the process.", "children": [{"id": "519ac60b-dd80-4338-93f3-185a3971f783", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sound-image relationships", "children": [{"id": "7fc5be8e-db87-407e-bac0-a3f481be6805", "type": "concept", "title": "sync"}, {"id": "3739c4cc-607a-4e1d-aeb6-9da788964d44", "type": "concept", "title": "counterpoint"}, {"id": "7a39f383-6a3e-4807-b6d4-4f14b1f8f013", "type": "concept", "title": "sound bridge"}, {"id": "a083b5b5-6f12-4215-b66d-10586583e61f", "type": "concept", "title": "hit point"}, {"id": "c9339032-fe75-4f41-8a66-acbafed51182", "type": "concept", "title": "audio cue"}, {"id": "8f175ae5-9b45-468a-82e2-f1e4e686c626", "type": "concept", "title": "silence"}], "description": "Students analyze how sound can reinforce, contrast, lead, or transform visual movement."}, {"id": "34f96fd7-da37-4572-8cfa-9fd3669e3d49", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Voiceover and narration workflow", "children": [{"id": "522d183d-b548-426a-b781-13ead0181fe0", "type": "concept", "title": "scratch track"}, {"id": "627f50f8-fe76-43dd-8083-fd665cf3fd6c", "type": "concept", "title": "voiceover"}, {"id": "096b1edf-15ef-47f9-b7a5-cc1890774764", "type": "concept", "title": "read rate"}, {"id": "a8dcfdff-1463-4325-be84-44b7b27dbbe5", "type": "concept", "title": "audio edit"}, {"id": "066945e3-2e72-498f-8985-6e00b6cf4c19", "type": "concept", "title": "caption timing"}, {"id": "cc2c1f2e-516c-4031-8b28-8bc8de5c09a4", "type": "concept", "title": "room tone"}], "description": "This subtopic covers script timing, scratch audio, performance, captioning, and pacing against voice."}, {"id": "9d0a98f1-2d03-47a7-808b-ab5c826793c3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Music and effects design", "children": [{"id": "81e906ff-5fbb-451f-b906-b231f50b52b2", "type": "concept", "title": "music bed"}, {"id": "9b0eebac-7e94-404e-93bb-8f9a24649e0a", "type": "concept", "title": "sound effect"}, {"id": "04e3d6e3-41d5-40ba-8b34-a21dc5a7402c", "type": "concept", "title": "whoosh"}, {"id": "0af241aa-2197-4231-aac4-6f0e4c926b7a", "type": "concept", "title": "impact"}, {"id": "44ab07b5-c52b-4377-ba58-135f38cd2c4e", "type": "concept", "title": "tempo map"}, {"id": "1e4ce7ad-f3af-4407-a870-e1e80e7cb75f", "type": "concept", "title": "mix level"}], "description": "Students build rhythmic edits and sound effects that support brand, story, and tactile motion."}]}, {"id": "0ea8e828-0258-4ab8-9e8a-785388602b7e", "type": "topic", "title": "Storyboarding, Style Frames, Animatics, and Previsualization", "description": "Strong motion work is planned before it is animated. This unit develops the preproduction documents that align concept, client, timing, and production.", "children": [{"id": "10331775-3bff-46db-a2b8-5dc30ef44285", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Storyboards and shot planning", "children": [{"id": "77bb1bf5-1715-4c1d-a55b-e6375843594f", "type": "concept", "title": "thumbnail"}, {"id": "d8d8de59-4c5d-41b1-a02c-200cf822a955", "type": "concept", "title": "storyboard panel"}, {"id": "dcd65545-63ac-449d-8061-5fb1d5568d88", "type": "concept", "title": "shot description"}, {"id": "d7696961-31b0-49a6-a41c-bc40a98e4a21", "type": "concept", "title": "transition note"}, {"id": "85631efd-b1e8-4d4b-ad50-31467cbced79", "type": "concept", "title": "camera move"}, {"id": "89e43c7b-04e1-4082-a6ce-8c5380db7cf5", "type": "concept", "title": "screen direction"}], "description": "Students translate scripts and concepts into visual sequences with clear actions, transitions, and screen states."}, {"id": "43be6f08-7285-4601-af9a-0e31bc40f20e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Style frames and design approval", "children": [{"id": "d700eed6-b3bf-430e-b1e7-a4d62267b9cd", "type": "concept", "title": "hero frame"}, {"id": "d6773d37-c821-4155-852c-738a1d7863f6", "type": "concept", "title": "style tile"}, {"id": "18e6f6a4-b524-4deb-9237-7f43c43349d5", "type": "concept", "title": "key visual"}, {"id": "89e9fbb5-2a25-4d03-b1b1-cc113659c9a5", "type": "concept", "title": "typographic system"}, {"id": "3084ceb2-4a52-4b5c-99fb-18c0046a5d67", "type": "concept", "title": "palette"}, {"id": "1837dd1b-d813-4aa8-a491-d342cc039602", "type": "concept", "title": "texture treatment"}], "description": "This subtopic uses polished stills to communicate the look and design system before animation labor begins."}, {"id": "21af7982-7321-4e17-9fa0-1ddc5fc6c19b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Animatics and timing tests", "children": [{"id": "04ae6fc3-5e6b-429e-85ea-7b4ac186e94e", "type": "concept", "title": "animatic"}, {"id": "46188e92-8b9d-46cf-8465-afa36ef1c43c", "type": "concept", "title": "scratch audio"}, {"id": "a94ab1b7-e454-4f3e-9f26-8d5b362a27cf", "type": "concept", "title": "timing pass"}, {"id": "8dbb1507-1bfb-4af5-b4fc-634000ffb7b7", "type": "concept", "title": "temp music"}, {"id": "751b906f-7032-462f-91e0-b691affff8f8", "type": "concept", "title": "rough cut"}, {"id": "9e528905-57d4-4d1c-8da4-bf4b18fd9f36", "type": "concept", "title": "approval milestone"}], "description": "Students test pacing, narration, music, and transitions using rough motion before final production."}]}, {"id": "823e9de6-c3ee-4cd9-86ea-512ac885453e", "type": "topic", "title": "2D/3D Hybrid Motion and Spatial Design", "description": "Modern motion design often blends 2D graphics, simulated depth, cameras, 3D objects, and spatial interfaces. This unit introduces those hybrid workflows.", "children": [{"id": "8fdd4643-7f01-45ba-b503-a9700f22ca56", "type": "subtopic", "title": "2.5D space and cameras", "children": [{"id": "ab2cbb0e-ebca-43b7-bf21-51c8573ebbf3", "type": "concept", "title": "3D layer"}, {"id": "ea279ec4-ab22-4b0b-aa14-57c5f134e8ae", "type": "concept", "title": "camera"}, {"id": "f5c54c39-cb0e-4cb8-b8cc-b4539fc1568e", "type": "concept", "title": "null object"}, {"id": "7a533256-1ce3-4baa-8ed3-181751599c10", "type": "concept", "title": "parallax"}, {"id": "121dd2cc-4f57-4a24-a1cb-deae0f9f26b7", "type": "concept", "title": "depth of field"}, {"id": "3d3a2733-f0da-469b-ac1c-b6d56945b0bb", "type": "concept", "title": "parenting"}], "description": "Students learn to create depth and movement using layers, cameras, lights, parallax, and perspective."}, {"id": "41e5a359-d154-4138-81fc-c5f35437125c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "3D objects and rendered assets", "children": [{"id": "b64e2d0c-cd36-4d1d-aeb5-df8be7b6bfc6", "type": "concept", "title": "model import"}, {"id": "8e9a1c47-2f9f-40c8-89bb-eec6255bdf87", "type": "concept", "title": "render pass"}, {"id": "422b859b-7baf-4ac2-99f2-8178a437625d", "type": "concept", "title": "lighting pass"}, {"id": "e22cd627-5324-4815-bc37-295d85b046f4", "type": "concept", "title": "material"}, {"id": "624f4686-76d7-47a5-935a-31d1deb0a6ad", "type": "concept", "title": "shadow"}, {"id": "edfe601f-a945-4c64-a720-1614950f8b02", "type": "concept", "title": "composite"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces how 3D models, renders, and passes can support motion graphics without turning the course into a full 3D class."}, {"id": "2542f714-6454-4458-ac5d-ddf80e858c10", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Spatial and installation contexts", "children": [{"id": "0fb630fd-af83-4b81-b57c-9d9b20287470", "type": "concept", "title": "projection mapping"}, {"id": "7e0828bd-cdf3-4fe9-8e49-38a808eadcd5", "type": "concept", "title": "LED wall"}, {"id": "6e0e6235-6bb8-4566-b7b2-e6a27eecb198", "type": "concept", "title": "multi-screen"}, {"id": "11979000-a1d3-454c-9386-d9521a36aaef", "type": "concept", "title": "installation"}, {"id": "b99b9fb9-e7ab-4291-b829-a0188043a8f0", "type": "concept", "title": "spatial sequence"}, {"id": "5ba6040d-0bea-40fe-8e6e-701a1a11275f", "type": "concept", "title": "viewer position"}], "description": "Students connect motion graphics to projection, events, screens, galleries, and immersive environments."}]}, {"id": "5c5607b7-d40c-461a-9f59-8a8507c8bb82", "type": "topic", "title": "Expressions, Templates, and Procedural Motion Systems", "description": "Motion designers build systems, not just one-off animations. This unit introduces expressions, templates, and reusable rigs.", "children": [{"id": "a5173c3e-b5f6-421a-9db4-12f579298aea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Expression basics", "children": [{"id": "9c1fe8a0-61d6-4a14-a570-6ae5284fd1e4", "type": "concept", "title": "expression"}, {"id": "94ac8add-ecc5-43bf-9896-bc76c5d8c3e2", "type": "concept", "title": "pick whip"}, {"id": "c07e0802-b034-41ff-b2d0-71d501732e86", "type": "concept", "title": "loopOut"}, {"id": "2b7f3471-9f65-4fec-b564-1888cca1af66", "type": "concept", "title": "wiggle"}, {"id": "1531ddd1-4d99-4ce5-b205-82dcf988ebde", "type": "concept", "title": "valueAtTime"}, {"id": "29600778-a630-491e-83e6-16e6b2c43d88", "type": "concept", "title": "slider control"}], "description": "Students use simple expressions to automate loops, wiggles, delays, relationships, and repeated behaviors."}, {"id": "5651c056-7ff2-493c-b2f2-6661c507fb12", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reusable rigs and templates", "children": [{"id": "e5dfb4df-4cba-433e-82b1-6d0d776d2d70", "type": "concept", "title": "essential graphics"}, {"id": "8ab8f0db-3e9d-4d1d-8e46-82149552f6ec", "type": "concept", "title": "MOGRT"}, {"id": "064646a2-685b-41fc-816d-a222c771b00c", "type": "concept", "title": "controller layer"}, {"id": "722373f1-e955-47d6-a82c-af0f69f94ce6", "type": "concept", "title": "responsive time"}, {"id": "40d12a55-d28e-4b1d-a61a-49599f939b64", "type": "concept", "title": "template field"}, {"id": "687bd29a-87ef-464e-bf25-abf1c412d23c", "type": "concept", "title": "protected region"}], "description": "This subtopic focuses on editable systems for lower thirds, social templates, brand packages, and repeated outputs."}, {"id": "dc7ba69d-3ce8-4a49-a50d-bce1990e0294", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Efficiency and consistency", "children": [{"id": "259f5b9d-5089-42a7-b42d-52d65bee6ec2", "type": "concept", "title": "modular comp"}, {"id": "0c3eb07c-0277-40a4-96ed-9df22777b1ba", "type": "concept", "title": "style control"}, {"id": "b3f4f79c-26f8-4cdc-a5c0-8382daafe0e7", "type": "concept", "title": "batch output"}, {"id": "57cbdb09-6e03-4def-8cb9-f1caf15bfe8d", "type": "concept", "title": "documentation"}, {"id": "1929cef3-26e4-423d-b662-79a5954186cc", "type": "concept", "title": "handoff"}, {"id": "8680656c-5bcd-48ce-b322-8bbe94ccd311", "type": "concept", "title": "quality control"}], "description": "Students learn to reduce production errors through systems thinking, naming, modular comps, and documentation."}]}, {"id": "3fb98749-b9bc-4553-b7ef-2943b39eea5e", "type": "topic", "title": "UI Motion, Microinteractions, and Product Animation", "description": "Motion graphics increasingly intersects with product design. This unit covers movement that clarifies interface state, feedback, hierarchy, and usability.", "children": [{"id": "e82254d6-c540-4481-b153-e0e40942e186", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Principles of UI motion", "children": [{"id": "08441c22-af23-4341-a262-a6b072dc935c", "type": "concept", "title": "state change"}, {"id": "c1fb5099-a0a0-486c-9317-d7edca8fc24e", "type": "concept", "title": "feedback"}, {"id": "bcdfbfac-d0ea-4570-859d-4a0da28af1f4", "type": "concept", "title": "affordance"}, {"id": "1153b70f-d109-4974-8e82-ea5d2ece8d23", "type": "concept", "title": "continuity"}, {"id": "11d7ccfe-b40a-4a71-82a1-c87f84f4eff1", "type": "concept", "title": "transition pattern"}, {"id": "945b0161-7288-4e6b-8388-6225b43b9eca", "type": "concept", "title": "microinteraction"}], "description": "Students learn how motion supports orientation, feedback, causality, and continuity in digital products."}, {"id": "b5d2a663-0457-4963-8d4b-6962fe66218e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prototype-to-production thinking", "children": [{"id": "46b72a2b-815d-4c65-ad19-ee1