position, Rhythm, and Hierarchy", "description": "Motion graphics still depend on graphic design fundamentals. This unit strengthens composition, contrast, hierarchy, color, rhythm, and continuity across moving frames.", "children": [{"id": "534fda3c-7b0b-49f3-ad6d-bfc342022c36", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Frame composition and staging", "children": [{"id": "ce07477a-4837-4ef1-93b4-54319b714e80", "type": "concept", "title": "staging"}, {"id": "230eccc0-8e6a-4fa8-8e11-97c0a004fca9", "type": "concept", "title": "focal point"}, {"id": "b2d64151-e572-4b18-b68f-4bd1f3bf6a37", "type": "concept", "title": "rule of thirds"}, {"id": "fed247f2-eb54-495c-aa0a-07a5d611ace0", "type": "concept", "title": "balance"}, {"id": "0696d833-8faf-4268-840a-48ded7e796fa", "type": "concept", "title": "negative space"}, {"id": "e4703975-db94-4efa-a5db-f3def7c743d2", "type": "concept", "title": "frame edge"}], "description": "Students design frames that guide attention before, during, and after movement."}, {"id": "67043e5f-4770-4ffb-92b6-48a159d743ef", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual rhythm and continuity", "children": [{"id": "36f21d44-a8f8-44c1-af71-0136738093fd", "type": "concept", "title": "visual rhythm"}, {"id": "d43e3d25-9a5b-49ea-8419-1db58da63854", "type": "concept", "title": "repetition"}, {"id": "e7a88c3e-3d91-4539-99d9-62cd5c4449f8", "type": "concept", "title": "contrast"}, {"id": "eb81f466-db27-4ba1-bfd6-2613206e5e6f", "type": "concept", "title": "continuity"}, {"id": "c73afcb9-0adc-4356-9740-3f963c96adae", "type": "concept", "title": "match movement"}, {"id": "8d025ac7-f20c-43cc-9f1e-fb3a10d6e960", "type": "concept", "title": "screen direction"}], "description": "This subtopic explores how repeated forms, cuts, entrances, and exits create a coherent viewing experience."}, {"id": "514896ec-f7bb-4088-9a2a-2c2cf810bb11", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color, texture, and style frames", "children": [{"id": "d47fad06-43bc-40a8-8d37-88dc9b904639", "type": "concept", "title": "style frame"}, {"id": "90b34846-bb38-487a-9e01-09b302bd183c", "type": "concept", "title": "color palette"}, {"id": "2fd3a8dd-a665-43d9-8a54-18e91a3d22fb", "type": "concept", "title": "texture"}, {"id": "53476b3f-a496-4b30-a612-01538ed9225d", "type": "concept", "title": "look development"}, {"id": "f9cd91ae-c036-46bf-8e93-029b48214428", "type": "concept", "title": "art direction"}, {"id": "22c7b539-2f2e-496a-bb7f-f4f21bca4f42", "type": "concept", "title": "mood board"}], "description": "Students use style frames to define look, mood, palette, typography, and visual language before animation begins."}]}, {"id": "22f979a2-f1eb-4bb1-b19f-a07900f605a9", "type": "topic", "title": "After Effects Workflow and Digital Production Basics", "description": "This unit develops fluency in After Effects and related production workflows so students can build organized, editable, and export-ready motion projects.", "children": [{"id": "6e9cebe7-5313-4984-b140-3d88afbd50d3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project organization", "children": [{"id": "44e6ae3f-ec7a-498c-9229-90ebf7e5bf81", "type": "concept", "title": "project panel"}, {"id": "66868028-e60a-40fe-a0d3-b349782cfe84", "type": "concept", "title": "composition"}, {"id": "e8ef9039-a39b-4581-a7a5-284d1d4991f1", "type": "concept", "title": "precomp"}, {"id": "19e7315b-1fd8-40d4-95f6-1cc05d3e2e87", "type": "concept", "title": "naming convention"}, {"id": "82477397-d413-4701-bb83-d42cb41dceeb", "type": "concept", "title": "asset folder"}, {"id": "134051f2-adbe-4682-b82b-ce6a00edfc31", "type": "concept", "title": "versioning"}], "description": "Students learn file hygiene, folder structure, naming, precomps, and version control for complex motion work."}, {"id": "2714425e-a194-4fdf-900c-84f15fc4e45a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Layers, keyframes, and graph editing", "children": [{"id": "18ad0f17-b4bb-42da-b299-566a7b23933a", "type": "concept", "title": "layer"}, {"id": "fadb85ba-3a90-40f6-a501-ec68d574020a", "type": "concept", "ti